{"availability":"available","full":"mazzucci/search-esque","name":"search-esque","description":"Elasticsearch-compatible query DSL and aggregations over SQLite","category":"Other","language":"Rust","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-11T01:26:25Z","updated":"2026-10-11T03:45:30Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://mazzucci.github.io/search-esque/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T05:14:43.284Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T05:14:43.284Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T05:14:43.284Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T06:14:43.839Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-17T05:14:43.284Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Elasticsearch-compatible query DSL and aggregations over SQLite.","Write the query you already know, bool, term, range, match, aggs with terms and datehistogram, and run it over a plain SQLite file. No search engine, no extension, no server. The same crate compiles to a native binary, to WebAssembly for the browser, and to a Python extension.","Why SQLite only: this is for light, local, throwaway data. The index is one file, facets are exact counts, and nothing you do here can hammer a shared database server with aggregation queries. A .db on a laptop, or in a browser tab, is the whole deployment."],"features":["term on a keyword field ignores letter case.","A quoted number for a number field is refused, not coerced.","Counts are exact, never approximate. terms has no shardsize.","should is supported only directly in a bool; minimumshouldmatch beyond 0 and 1 is refused.","With no sort, hits come back in id order."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mazzucci/search-esque/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"667536d4a97ca3aee376863d57566b0a495615b5d4517a19957e756d5df6c66d","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T06:14:43.955Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T06:14:43.955Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Elasticsearch-c